      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:6:2:6",
      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) عَنْ لَحْمِ الْكَلْبِ فَقَالَ هُوَ مَسْخٌ قُلْتُ هُوَ حَرَامٌ قَالَ هُوَ نَجَسٌ أُعِيدُهَا عَلَيْهِ ثَلَاثَ مَرَّاتٍ كُلَّ ذَلِكَ يَقُولُ هُوَ نَجَسٌ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "A number of our companions, from Sahl Bin Ziyad, from Ibn Abu Najran, from Aasim Bin Humeyd, from Abu Sahl Al Qurshy who said, ",
          "‘I asked Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> about meat of the dog. So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘It is a morphed (creature)’. I said, ‘It is Prohibited?’ He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘It is unclean’. I re-iterated over it three times, during each of that he<sup>asws</sup> was saying: ‘It is unclean’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "6. A number of our people have narrated from Sahl ibn Ziyad from ibn abu Najran from ‘Asem ibn Hamid from abu Sahl al-Qarashiy who has said the following: “I once asked abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about the flesh of dogs. He (the Imam) said, ‘It is metamorphosed.’ I asked, ‘Is it unlawful for food?’ He (the Imam) said, ‘It is Najis (unclean). I repeat it three times for you and each one says it is Najis (unclean).”’ "
        ]
      }
    },
